<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aktekke Mosque</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1370s</span> · Also known as Mader-i Mevlana Mosque</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aktekke Mosque is a 14th-century mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaman">Karaman</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, built under the Karamanid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaeddin-bey">Alaeddin Bey</a> on the site of an earlier dervish lodge. It is linked to the family of the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rumi">Rumi</a>, whose mother is traditionally said to be buried there, and is also known as the Mader-i Mevlana Mosque. It is one of the main surviving monuments of the Karamanid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>.</p></div>
